@attribute [Route("/components/" + nameof(HxAlert))]

<ApiDoc Type="typeof(HxAlert)">
    <DocHeading Title="Basic usage" />
    <p>
        The alert is a flex container, each child element becomes a flex item (separated by a gap).
        Wrap the text, including any inline elements such as links or <code>&lt;strong&gt;</code>, in a <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> element,
        otherwise the text and the inline elements are laid out as separate flex items.
    </p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxAlert_Demo_Basic)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Default alert" Level="3" />
    <p>Without the <code>Color</code> parameter, the alert renders with the neutral (default) colors.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxAlert_Demo_Default)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Link color" />
    <p>Use the <code>.alert-link</code> class on links inside an alert to quickly provide matching colored links.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxAlert_Demo_LinkColor)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Icons" />
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxAlert_Demo_Icons)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Additional content" />
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxAlert_Demo_AdditionalContent)" Tabs="false" />

	<DocHeading Title="Dismissible" />
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxAlert_Demo_Dismissible)" Tabs="false" />
    <p>
        When dismissed, the alert is removed from the page. If a keyboard user dismisses the alert using the close button, their focus is lost.
        Use the <code>OnClosed</code> callback to stop rendering the alert and to move focus to the most appropriate location in the page.
    </p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxAlert_Demo_OnClosed)" />
</ApiDoc>
